id: VS-03
name: Risk Analysis
short_description: Produce evidence-based understanding of exposure and drivers to
  support prioritisation and treatment design.
owner: null
stakeholders:
- Risk Owners, Risk Function, Finance, Security/Ops SMEs, ExCo/Board (for material
  risks)
triggers:
- Material risks, critical service reviews, board deep dives, initiative gates, appetite
  breaches.
inputs:
- Risk records (VS-02), appetite/criteria (VS-00), control data (VS-06), KRI data
  (VS-07), loss/incidents (VS-09).
entry_criteria: ''
key_activities:
- '1) Select analysis technique (tiered: quick qualification → detailed scenario)'
- 2) Assess inherent likelihood/impact
- 3) Assess control design and operating effectiveness
- 4) Compute residual risk and confidence
- 5) Quantify exposure where required (ranges/scenarios)
- 6) Perform sensitivity/uncertainty review
- 7) Document evidence and assumptions
- 8) Submit for challenge/approval
decisions_and_gates: []
outputs:
- Inherent/residual ratings, scenario analysis artefacts, quantified exposure bands,
  assumptions and evidence logs.
exit_criteria: ''
metrics: 'Flow: assessment cycle time; rework rate after challenge; WIP of assessments.<br>Performance:
  assessment QA score; % with evidence; consistency across BUs.<br>Risk: % material
  risks with quantified view (where policy requires); override frequency.'
source_file: docs\value-architecture\value-streams\VS-03-risk-analysis.md
last_updated: '2026-02-01T12:57:08.961004Z'
